# Zig build-system cache: build graph, compiler intermediates, codegen
# scratch. Everything in here is content-hash keyed and fully regenerated
# by `zig build`, so it is never worth committing.
.zig-cache/
zig-cache/

# Install prefix written by `zig build` / `zig build install`
# (zig-out/bin/rticz, zig-out/bin/rticz-cli). Regenerate instead of commit.
zig-out/

# Local package cache populated by `zig fetch` (older workflow; harmless
# to keep listed for projects that grow dependencies).
.deps/

# Emitted build artifacts.  The hand-written codegen tools live in
# codegen/ (committed, framework-owned); each application package's
# generated/ holds only what they emit — the vector table and the
# per-task contexts — so the whole folder is ignored: the application's
# `zig build` rewrites these files on every run, and committing them
# would only invite stale copies.  They are placed in the source tree,
# not the build cache, so the emitted table and contexts stay readable
# as-is; the generators recreate the folder itself, which is why it may
# be absent entirely.  (A `zig fetch`ed application package would also
# not ship its own generated/ for the same reason — this pattern, with
# no leading slash, matches at any depth.)
generated/

# Editor / OS cruft.
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
